# Whole-year print for 2026 (per the User Instructions above and the B-row
# cue-card example: key year, press A, key months, R/S, key start month,
# R/S). Data entry and the print itself all run at full speed — this used to
# run far slower than real time at full speed (the ROM's fast-mode print
# dispatcher retries its own key/printer-busy poll in a tight spin outside
# the normal keyboard-scan idle loop, and the full-speed throttle didn't
# recognize it), inflating the reported elapsed time 9x over the
# regular-speed figure. Fixed by having TMC0501::step() flag a confirmed
# poll-retry spin by opcode pattern rather than by ROM address (see
# TMC0501.hpp's step() doc comment and EmulatorViewModel.swift's
# startEmulationLoop()) — full speed now reports the same elapsed time as
# regular speed for this print job.
FullSpeed:
83              # 2
92              # 0
83              # 2
74              # 6
11              # A — store starting year 2026
82              # 1
83              # 2              → 12 months
91              # R/S
82              # 1              → start month 1
ZeroElapseTime:
91              # R/S — print the whole year, full speed
ReportElapseTime:
RegularSpeed:
